{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1487577-victorian-mage-if-no-society-of-ether-then-who","id":1487577,"title":"Victorian Mage: if no Society of Ether, then who?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-07-23T06:17:47-07:00","id":1487577,"title":"Victorian Mage: if no Society of Ether, then who?","content":"In Victorian Mage, there's a Future Fate addressing the Ether. One of the alternate futures described is one where the nascent Technocracy accepts the Ether, and the Society of Ether never leaves the fold. It goes on to suggest that the Council of Magick would seek a ninth Tradition among the Crafts, and that they'd eventually settle on the Kopa Loei. <br /> <br /> Why? First, they've been a Council of Eight ever since the Solificati left at the end of the Sorcerers Crusade. Why the sudden urgency to take just anyone to fill the vacancy? And second, why the Kopa Loei? Why not, for instance, the Ngoma? <br /> <br /> I'm not just picking a name or of a hat here. The Ngoma are described in M20 as being borderline technomancers. As well, they're of the same cultural roots as the Wamukamwami, a Central/Southern African society that Victorian Mage suggests might have a better handle on Ether Science than the Etherites do. If we integrate the Wamukamwami into the Ngoma as one of its factions and play up the techno- side of the Craft, I submit that that would be a <i>much</i> better fit for the empty seat on the Council than the Kopa Loei. <br /> <br /> And besides, the Ngoma didn't reject the Traditions back during the Sorcerers Crusade when they were invited to join. They <i>liked</i> the idea of the Traditions, but refused to be lumped in with the Dreamspeakers, holding out for full Tradition status in their own right and leaving only after it was apparent that it wasn't going to happen. So if the Council suddenly, after four centuries, starts looking to fill the empty seat, I think the Ngoma would be at least open to the idea. <br /> <br /> And of course, that still leaves the question of why the Council would wait for centuries to ask. Though there, I could see the birth of the Technocracy being the trigger. <br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-23T07:46:54-07:00","id":1487587,"title":"","content":"Cultural changes over four centuries can help. Although we use the word &quot;Orientalism&quot; in an extremely negative way, the Orientalists were the real start of multiculturalism. Orientalists held that other cultures outside the West were not just worthy of study but were vital to understanding humanity. Although we now link Orientalism with colonialism and racism this is a complete reversal of history. Orientalists were among the first important voices in the West to challenge both imperialism and the &quot;Scientific Racism&quot; popular in the 19th century. Our present negative view of Orientalists comes from the cheap nihilism of the 1970s. <br /> <br /> Because of the Orientalists, and groups like the Order of Hermes researching their deep roots, I could see the Hermetics simply coming to realize they'd been wrong. After the disaster of the Verbena, the Dreamspeakers, and the Cult of Ecstasy's failed outreach to the Bata'as, the Hermetics, hat in hand, go to the Ngoma with apologies and an invitation. <br /> <br /> These factors would explain the timing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-23T09:57:49-07:00","id":1487611,"title":"","content":"I agree with Astromancer, and yes the Ngoma would be a fine addtion.<br /> <br /> I cannot however live in a world with no Etherites. They are my favorite Trad, and a world without them is akin to heresy in my book hehe","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-23T10:00:57-07:00","id":1487612,"title":"","content":"Also, we have to truly think what would the consequences be for the Technocratic Paradigm if the Ether Theory got adopted. There would be no Relativity, no Quantum Theory. What would it be of Dimension Science in such a case? How would that affect their time table and the modern world?<br /> <br /> This is no small change. The modern world would become a serious alternate history parallel, with significant technological changes","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-23T10:44:19-07:00","id":1487620,"title":"","content":"Indeed. You'd still have your Sons of Ether; it's just that they'd still be in the ranks of the Technocracy. <br /> <br /> Which implies even more drastic changes to the setting; because if the Technocracy adopted Ether Science, the \u201cOne Truth\u201d philosophy that defines them so much today would have lost out. Basically, the Technocracy would effectively be <i>replaced by</i> the Society of Ether, in all but name. For the most part. <br /> <br /> And again, there's the Wamukamwami faction within the Ngoma, who bring their own brand of Ether Science to the Traditions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-23T15:48:00-07:00","id":1487657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1487577-victorian-mage-if-no-society-of-ether-then-who?p=1487620#post1487620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed. You'd still have your Sons of Ether; it's just that they'd still be in the ranks of the Technocracy. <br /> <br /> Which implies even more drastic changes to the setting; because if the Technocracy adopted Ether Science, the \u201cOne Truth\u201d philosophy that defines them so much today would have lost out. Basically, the Technocracy would effectively be <i>replaced by</i> the Society of Ether, in all but name. For the most part. <br /> <br /> And again, there's the Wamukamwami faction within the Ngoma, who bring their own brand of Ether Science to the Traditions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just imagine that, perhaps an even more radical &quot;Quantum Theory&quot; that says that the &quot;principle of the observer&quot; is not related to some subatomic particles interation or any such &quot;nonsense&quot;, but rather is reliant on a REAL <b>concious</b> observer... And modern technology would become a crazy thing! Just imagine sleepers &quot;praying&quot; or meditating in order to make their computers work... Thing like the &quot;Attraction Law&quot; being thought at schools... It would be crazy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-23T16:03:57-07:00","id":1487659,"title":"","content":"Frankly, I'm hoping to find somewhere some explanation on just what Victorian Mage meant when it said that the Wamukamwami might possibly have a better understanding of Ether Mechanics than the Sons of Ether. What exactly is the Wamukamwami Paradigms, Practices, and Instruments, and how do they fit together?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T05:08:15-07:00","id":1487867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1487577-victorian-mage-if-no-society-of-ether-then-who?p=1487659#post1487659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Frankly, I'm hoping to find somewhere some explanation on just what Victorian Mage meant when it said that the Wamukamwami might possibly have a better understanding of Ether Mechanics than the Sons of Ether. What exactly is the Wamukamwami Paradigms, Practices, and Instruments, and how do they fit together?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would they join the Ngoma and not the Etherites?<br /> <br /> And for your question, I cant answer that. Only the publishers can, or you create your own headcannon","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T05:24:09-07:00","id":1487873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1487577-victorian-mage-if-no-society-of-ether-then-who?p=1487867#post1487867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would they join the Ngoma and not the Etherites?</div> </div> </div> </div>Politics, basically. Remember, in this scenario, the Etherites never leave the Technocracy; and the Wamukamwami were persecuted by the Technocracy. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1487577-victorian-mage-if-no-society-of-ether-then-who?p=1487867#post1487867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And for your question, I cant answer that. Only the publishers can, or you create your own headcannon</div> </div> </div> </div>I was hoping that someone would know something about the real-world Wamukamwami that might explain why the writers of Victorian Mage for the idea that they might know something about the Ether.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T06:38:27-07:00","id":1487878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1487577-victorian-mage-if-no-society-of-ether-then-who?p=1487873#post1487873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was hoping that someone would know something about the real-world Wamukamwami that might explain why the writers of Victorian Mage for the idea that they might know something about the Ether.</div> </div> </div> </div>I found no references to it outside of WoD wikis, except as a word in either Bantu or Zulu and only in a single book that talks about Bantu folklore. Im afraid that this is not a real world group (or real word legend/myth), but rather a completely fictional group for WoD alone that the authors simply thought it would be a &quot;cool name&quot;. But it seems to lack any real substance otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T06:51:13-07:00","id":1487880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1487577-victorian-mage-if-no-society-of-ether-then-who?p=1487659#post1487659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Frankly, I'm hoping to find somewhere some explanation on just what Victorian Mage meant when it said that the Wamukamwami might possibly have a better understanding of Ether Mechanics than the Sons of Ether. What exactly is the Wamukamwami Paradigms, Practices, and Instruments, and how do they fit together?</div> </div> </div> </div>Are they just a one note throwaway line or do they get a writeup in the book?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T09:12:51-07:00","id":1487892,"title":"","content":"One note throwaway. What I've quoted in this thread is basically it. <br /> <br /> But these days, Onyx Path doesn't make up such things out of whole cloth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T10:22:10-07:00","id":1487907,"title":"","content":"Maybe a &quot;Companion&quot; addition? They seem to like these mini lines springing up around a kickstarter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T20:31:08-07:00","id":1487970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1487577-victorian-mage-if-no-society-of-ether-then-who?p=1487892#post1487892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One note throwaway. What I've quoted in this thread is basically it. <br /> <br /> But these days, Onyx Path doesn't make up such things out of whole cloth.</div> </div> </div> </div>This would appear to be the exception thou. Like I said, I only found one reference of it, and in a 500+ pages book about Bantu folklore. I obviously didnt read the entire book, but the term is only used twice and only in 2 sequential paragraphs, and in the context it seems to imply to mean &quot;charlatans&quot;, as in false shamans or priests that deceive others by posing as spiritual guides. And it certanly has absolutely zero connection to any sort of techno-fetishism or any such.<br /> <br /> I would say that, in this case, it were indeed completely taken completely out of the hat, with the sole purpose to generate drama (look, african etherites! Oh, but the big baddie Order of Reason utterly destroyed that seed before it could bear any fruits), and there was nothing more to them than being a historic footnote to create a sense of awe for the overall setting.<br /> <br /> Im sorry to being the bearer of ill news, but that's the ugly truth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-28T04:35:21-07:00","id":1488253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1487577-victorian-mage-if-no-society-of-ether-then-who?p=1487620#post1487620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed. You'd still have your Sons of Ether; it's just that they'd still be in the ranks of the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> Which implies even more drastic changes to the setting; because if the Technocracy adopted Ether Science, the \u201cOne Truth\u201d philosophy that defines them so much today would have lost out. Basically, the Technocracy would effectively be <i>replaced by</i> the Society of Ether, in all but name. For the most part.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Two other changes. The Etherites represent science pushed forward by the (usually wealthy) individual rather than the industrial cooperation of the current Technocracy. Debunking the Ether wasn't just about getting rid of a theory, it was about curbing the independent streak of a Convention and setting the rules for how scientific advancement in the next 200 years would work. <br /> <br /> Also, the Etherites are quite comfortable with authoritarianism, and were even more so before they were on the receiving end. If they were not rebuked but instead grew to become a full Convention, I would expect that fascist idealism streak to grow and influence the rest of the Technocracy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-28T05:24:36-07:00","id":1488256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1487577-victorian-mage-if-no-society-of-ether-then-who?p=1488253#post1488253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, the Etherites are quite comfortable with authoritarianism, and were even more so before they were on the receiving end. If they were not rebuked but instead grew to become a full Convention, I would expect that fascist idealism streak to grow and influence the rest of the Technocracy.</div> </div> </div> </div>What makes you say that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-28T06:55:16-07:00","id":1488258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1487577-victorian-mage-if-no-society-of-ether-then-who?p=1488256#post1488256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What makes you say that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Partly it is how they are tied in with a lot of golden age science fiction, which is thick with ideal societies lead by enlightened totalitarian scientists. Also, one of their most famous members, Czar Vargo, literally tried to take over the world and is celebrated for it. Note, I don't mean they tend towards a love of control and power, instead they tend towards justifying power grabs in the name of enlightened or altruistic ideals. Czar Vargo was trying to end WWI, for instance. The Technocracy considers itself to be working towards altruistic ends, though, and I think if the Etherites remained there they would have agreed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-28T07:03:07-07:00","id":1488260,"title":"","content":"Nitpick: Vargo wasn't trying to end WWI; it hadn't started yet. (If you look at the exact dates of things, his move to take over happened precisely halfway between the assassination of Archduke Ferdinand and the formal outbreak of hostilities.) It would be more fair to say that he was trying to <i>prevent</i> WWI. <br /> <br /> But as I said, that's a nitpick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 07-28-2022, 02:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-28T10:58:19-07:00","id":1488267,"title":"","content":"It should also be considered that Vargo is not celebrated for &quot;trying to take over the world&quot;. He's celebrated for being someone willing to make a great change and push the consensus no matter what the masses think, which is kinda what Ascension is about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-29T05:09:08-07:00","id":1488351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1487577-victorian-mage-if-no-society-of-ether-then-who?p=1488258#post1488258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Partly it is how they are tied in with a lot of golden age science fiction, which is thick with ideal societies lead by enlightened totalitarian scientists. Also, one of their most famous members, Czar Vargo, literally tried to take over the world and is celebrated for it. Note, I don't mean they tend towards a love of control and power, instead they tend towards justifying power grabs in the name of enlightened or altruistic ideals. Czar Vargo was trying to end WWI, for instance. The Technocracy considers itself to be working towards altruistic ends, though, and I think if the Etherites remained there they would have agreed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see. I dont view them as fascists - or, better saying, THEY dont view themselves as fascists.<br /> <br /> They are my personal favorite tradition, but of course they do display the worse traits of what I see in many real life intellectuals too, which is &quot;I know better&quot;. And yes, it is the sign of all fascist and commie tyrants ever, to believe themselves above the ignorant masses and to know what's better for everybody else, better than everybody else. Yes, I agree with you in that.<br /> <br /> This is a trait they share in common with the OoH, but it's not a coincidence, in my view the OoH has always been borderline Order of Reason. Or, the Order of Hermes was the Order of Reason before it was cool.<br /> <br /> It's a matter of Hubris. &quot;You're too dumb and ignorant to take care of yourself, therefore I have to take care of you for your own good&quot;.<br /> <br /> Here in Brazil we have the saying that is: by good intentions, the hell is filled.<br /> <br /> Fascists and commies always start with the good intentions of the &quot;enlightned&quot; ones that &quot;know better&quot;. This is a flaw of many of the real life intellectuals.<br /> <br /> Indeed, the Etherites are visionaries and they see themselves as the heroes of their stories, but a &quot;philosopher king&quot; by the end of the day is just a despot, no matter how &quot;enlightned&quot; he believes himself to be.<br /> <br /> That's a trait shared by Etherites, Order of Hermes and Technocracy, and it's a sign of their inflated hubris.<br /> <br /> Funny how it's a trait of those who believe themselves to be &quot;free thinkers&quot;, such as those 3, or the &quot;rational&quot; ones, the 3 groups who are most devoted to logic and reason as opposed to a more &quot;spiritual&quot; balance, a more mystic approach. Chakravanti, Akashic, Ecstatics, Verbena, Corists and even the VA are much less prone to those pitfalls because they are much more tolerant of creativity and spiritual development rather than rigid rationalism as the previous 3 groups","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-29T08:08:35-07:00","id":1488361,"title":"","content":"I once ran an alternate history mage game (Very briefly) where the Sons of Ether, Difference Engineers, and Explorators made their own faction;<br /> leaving the Technocracy with the NWO, ITX, Progenitors, and Syndicate<br /> In that setting<br /> the Solificati managed to retain their place in the Traditions by renouncing Helyel and gaining something like a extremely strict view of loyalty to the traditions<br /> and the Ahli Batin retained their seat as well.<br /> <br /> In that setting, no one group had dominance and things became very steampunk/dieselpunk pulp fiction","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12480,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","user":"Spacecat","date":". 07-29-2022, 11:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-29T09:56:32-07:00","id":1488370,"title":"","content":"The Solificati <i>are</i> another possibility, yes. They have a history that closely mirrors that of the Etherites, to the point that there's a tendency to conflate them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-29T15:09:46-07:00","id":1488396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1487577-victorian-mage-if-no-society-of-ether-then-who?p=1488351#post1488351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...and even the VA are much less prone to those pitfalls because they are much more tolerant of creativity and spiritual development rather than rigid rationalism as the previous 3 groups</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to disagree or anything, but I was reading Masters of the Art the other day, and in that a character pretty much argues the opposite. That the Adepts are actually well on their way to becoming just like the OoH. A hierarchy where power is the only determination of worthiness. (Admittedly it's phrased in late 90s leet speak, which makes a bit less threatening, but it gels with the way the actual California Ideology people have gone).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-29T15:15:28-07:00","id":1488397,"title":"","content":"To be fair, I'm not sure that the actual California people would qualify as VAs. They strike me as the digital frontier of the NWO and/or Syndicate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-29T16:09:19-07:00","id":1488402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1487577-victorian-mage-if-no-society-of-ether-then-who?p=1488397#post1488397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, I'm not sure that the actual California people would qualify as VAs. They strike me as the digital frontier of the NWO and/or Syndicate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely, but then there aren't really any California Ideology people left.<br /> <br /> Sorry to divert the threat further, but I do think it would have been interesting to see the VAs follow their real life inspirations, having them return to the Technocracy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-29T19:16:42-07:00","id":1488429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1487577-victorian-mage-if-no-society-of-ether-then-who?p=1488396#post1488396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not to disagree or anything, but I was reading Masters of the Art the other day, and in that a character pretty much argues the opposite. That the Adepts are actually well on their way to becoming just like the OoH. A hierarchy where power is the only determination of worthiness. (Admittedly it's phrased in late 90s leet speak, which makes a bit less threatening, but it gels with the way the actual California Ideology people have gone).</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the California guys are actually the Iteration X and NWO techies, not the VAs.<br /> <br /> The VAs of REAL LIFE are more like the Cypherpunks who created Bitcoin and groups such as anonimous. The Cypherpunks by the way looks pretty Anarcho Capitalists (and this added to the fact they invented Bitcoin makes them my personal anonimous heroes).<br /> <br /> Sure, that all depends wether or not the &quot;Big Brother&quot; behind Google, Microsoft, Facebook, IBM and the rest of the big techs are run by the VAs or by technocrats.<br /> <br /> What do you think? Does Mark Censorbag of FakeTube is a VA or a techno fascist? I lean more towards the technocracy than the VAs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-29T19:27:27-07:00","id":1488431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1487577-victorian-mage-if-no-society-of-ether-then-who?p=1488402#post1488402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Absolutely, but then there aren't really any California Ideology people left.<br /> <br /> Sorry to divert the threat further, but I do think it would have been interesting to see the VAs follow their real life inspirations, having them return to the Technocracy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree. I see the VAs to be EXACTLY were they belong, flipping the bird to the big boss.<br /> <br /> You'd be impressed about just how many people that work in the field of information technologies are actually ancaps. It's anecdotal observation, sure, but the impression I get is that it's the field with the highest amount of ancaps.<br /> <br /> You get people in the area making projects for descentralized internet of all kinds, doing their best to prevent the &quot;Big Brother&quot; from completely taking over. Bitcoin for example was <i>probably</i> created by a group of programers members of the movement self entitled &quot;cypherpunks&quot;. You do have SEVERAL groups of hacker activists who on many ocasions risk jail, doing what they do based purely on ideological ideas of freedom and liberty from the clutches of the government. This is what inspired the Anonimous movement too. <br /> <br /> All those real life hacker activists are what inspired the VAs, and they actually may be the group with the best real life connection; I would say that the VA are more &quot;realistic&quot; than the Etherites, of course, but even more so than the Celestial Chorus, Verbena, even more than the OoH themselves.<br /> <br /> I dont usually pick them up, but I think they are awesome and have an incredible niche","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-30T05:03:59-07:00","id":1488452,"title":"","content":"I think that if we're rethinking of the Virtual Adepts for the modern age, we need to embrace the fact that they will consist of unsavoury tech moguls, billionare philantropists, the old fashioned Hack the Planet - Information Wants to be free, psychic masters of the digital age, influencer kingpins and the aging cyberpunks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-01T03:51:33-07:00","id":1488681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1487577-victorian-mage-if-no-society-of-ether-then-who?p=1488351#post1488351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I see. I dont view them as fascists - or, better saying, THEY dont view themselves as fascists.<br /> <br /> They are my personal favorite tradition, but of course they do display the worse traits of what I see in many real life intellectuals too, which is &quot;I know better&quot;. And yes, it is the sign of all fascist and commie tyrants ever, to believe themselves above the ignorant masses and to know what's better for everybody else, better than everybody else. Yes, I agree with you in that.<br /> <br /> ...<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's why I said authoritarian and totalitarian. I don't think they tend towards fascism as an ethos. Instead they are prone to say that &quot;Things would be much better if everyone did X&quot; and then consider coercion and authority as viable means to get everyone to do X. A few would even say &quot;Things would be so much better if everyone <i>were</i> X&quot; and act accordingly, though that's rare in the current Traditions version of the Etherites. It is much more an NWO thing. If they never left the Technocracy, though, I think it would be much more pronounced. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-01T04:49:11-07:00","id":1488682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1487577-victorian-mage-if-no-society-of-ether-then-who?p=1488681#post1488681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's why I said authoritarian and totalitarian. I don't think they tend towards fascism as an ethos. Instead they are prone to say that &amp;quot;Things would be much better if everyone did X&amp;quot; and then consider coercion and authority as viable means to get everyone to do X. A few would even say &amp;quot;Things would be so much better if everyone <i>were</i> X&amp;quot; and act accordingly, though that's rare in the current Traditions version of the Etherites. It is much more an NWO thing. If they never left the Technocracy, though, I think it would be much more pronounced. <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, I fully agree. &quot;It's for the greater good&quot; is usually at the root of most of the evils in the world. I absolutely love the Etherites and the Technocracy in the game, but in real life they would be everything I stand against. I dont like the VAs very much, maybe they are my least favorite tradition, but funnily their anarchic nature is probably the one that most closely align with my personal worldviews lol. Now I need to do some introspection to myself and try to understand why is that lol.<br /> <br /> In a sense thou, authoritarianism/totalitarianism seems to be a scourge that afflicts a good amount of Mages - if not ALL of them. The Order of Hermes is guilty of that, the Chakravanti are too, as are the Celestial Chorus... Pretty much ALL groups believe that &quot;everything would be better if they were done my way&quot;. That is, after all, the basic premisse of the Ascension War, the desire to impose one's own worldview on... everybody else. Mages are creatures of hubris, which is understandable for beings that can shape reality with their will. The downside to it is that it becomes &quot;my way or the high way&quot;.<br /> <br /> So... Maybe Mages are indeed THE WORST critters in the WoD, despite being the heroes of their own tales (and even the technocrats are heroes too). But &quot;by good intentions the hell is filled&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-01T06:05:50-07:00","id":1488690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1487577-victorian-mage-if-no-society-of-ether-then-who?p=1488681#post1488681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's why I said authoritarian and totalitarian. I don't think they tend towards fascism as an ethos. Instead they are prone to say that &quot;Things would be much better if everyone did X&quot; and then consider coercion and authority as viable means to get everyone to do X. A few would even say &quot;Things would be so much better if everyone <i>were</i> X&quot; and act accordingly, though that's rare in the current Traditions version of the Etherites. It is much more an NWO thing. If they never left the Technocracy, though, I think it would be much more pronounced.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's... pretty much the whole thesis of the Ascension War, and why there would be issues even if the Traditions were the ones in Charge. Ultimatley it's a battle for hearts, minds and beliefs, and everyone believes their own are superior.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-01T07:32:39-07:00","id":1488692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1487577-victorian-mage-if-no-society-of-ether-then-who?p=1488690#post1488690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's... pretty much the whole thesis of the Ascension War, and why there would be issues even if the Traditions were the ones in Charge. Ultimatley it's a battle for hearts, minds and beliefs, and everyone believes their own are superior.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not really? I mean, yes it is a battle for hearts and minds, but only some of the factions are interested in imposing their ideals by via authority. Even among those that do, totalitarianism is only one of many flavors of coercion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 08-01-2022, 10:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-01T08:12:03-07:00","id":1488698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1487577-victorian-mage-if-no-society-of-ether-then-who?p=1488692#post1488692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Not really? I mean, yes it is a battle for hearts and minds, but only some of the factions are interested in imposing their ideals by via authority. Even among those that do, totalitarianism is only one of many flavors of coercion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. I'd say that the Verbena, Akashic, Dreamspeakers, VAs and Ecstatics are more than willing to share their views and educate people about them, but do not wish to IMPOSE those. For the Chakravanti, Hermetics, Chorists and Etherites however, they do wish to do the &quot;greater good&quot; however.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-01T08:26:25-07:00","id":1488699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1487577-victorian-mage-if-no-society-of-ether-then-who?p=1488692#post1488692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Not really? I mean, yes it is a battle for hearts and minds, but only some of the factions are interested in imposing their ideals by via authority. Even among those that do, totalitarianism is only one of many flavors of coercion.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are still imposing your beliefs unto others and considering them as inferior to your own. Do you actually believe that the kind of personalities that make Mages are keen on doing it peacefully and live and let live?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-01T09:52:40-07:00","id":1488717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1487577-victorian-mage-if-no-society-of-ether-then-who?p=1488699#post1488699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You are still imposing your beliefs unto others and considering them as inferior to your own. Do you actually believe that the kind of personalities that make Mages are keen on doing it peacefully and live and let live?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mages are indeed creature of hubris. So much so that the Asncension War could just as easily be named &quot;the War of Hubris&quot;. Even the Dreamspeakers do indeed consider outsiders to be ignorant barbarians threatning the world with their stupidity.<br /> <br /> It's hard not to be like that thou... I mean, if I personally had seeing THE FREAKING TRUTH and awakened to it, how could I tolerate the short sightness and self destructive actions that are dragging us all down with their ignorant views and actions?<br /> <br /> The entire War of Ascension is a conflict between &quot;Im right, you are wrong, and your ignorant ways are harming us all, thus I MUST put a stop to them!&quot;.<br /> <br /> This holds true even before the Order of Reason; that's the cause of the Himalaian Wars between the Chakravanti and Akashics for instance. One trying to impose their views on the other and &quot;save them from themselves&quot;. Or the Chorists/Hermetics/Verbena conflicts.<br /> <br /> Mages are dicks! Total arseholes!<br /> <br /> People get disgusted at vampires, but Mages are the worse jerks of the WoD!<br /> <br /> And I love those magnificent bastards!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-01T09:59:51-07:00","id":1488718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1487577-victorian-mage-if-no-society-of-ether-then-who?p=1488717#post1488717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mages are dicks! Total arseholes!<br /> <br /> People get disgusted at vampires, but Mages are the worse jerks of the WoD!<br /> <br /> And I love those magnificent bastards!</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the thing. I'm not sure Mages are &quot;the worst jerks of the WoD&quot;<b>*</b>. Mages are human and by dint of that are prone to factionalism and tribalism. The kind of people that can be Mages are the kind of people that change the world, now if they only change it for their own selves and aim for personal and/or paradigmatic Ascension they are bound for conflict with others around them. That makes for great stories and the Ascension War is as good a framing as any to allow these conflicts to the fore. And yes, they can be great fun for gaming.<br /> <br /> However, there is a winning proposition here, one that may actually be the True Ascension of the game - the point where the goal isn't personal/paradigmatic Ascension, but the complete emancipation and Ascension of humankind. That may be the titular Ascension and the actual way how mankind gets better.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\"><b>*</b>I'm pretty sure that title goes to Vampires anyway</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-01T10:01:10-07:00","id":1488719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1487577-victorian-mage-if-no-society-of-ether-then-who?p=1488699#post1488699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You are still imposing your beliefs unto others and considering them as inferior to your own. Do you actually believe that the kind of personalities that make Mages are keen on doing it peacefully and live and let live?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That all Mages think their beliefs are superior to others is both universal and trivially true. If they didn't think that their beliefs were superior they'd believe something else. Even those few Mages dedicated to the idea that all beliefs are equally valid are doing it. After all, 'all beliefs are equally valid' is a belief and they are elevating it above 'not all beliefs are equally valid.' <br /> <br /> That said, just because Mages think their views are superior does not mean that they are authoritarian in how they spread them. As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24689\" data-vbnamecard=\"24689\">Kakost</a> said, sharing views and educating people is a method many Mages pursue and both of them *can* be done honestly and openly. The temptation to spread an idea in a heavy handed, imperialistic, or violent way is a constant temptation to Mages, I'll freely admit, but many Mages are morally and paradigmatically opposed to that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-01T10:16:36-07:00","id":1488721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1487577-victorian-mage-if-no-society-of-ether-then-who?p=1488719#post1488719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That all Mages think their beliefs are superior to others is both universal and trivially true. If they didn't think that their beliefs were superior they'd believe something else. Even those few Mages dedicated to the idea that all beliefs are equally valid are doing it. After all, 'all beliefs are equally valid' is a belief and they are elevating it above 'not all beliefs are equally valid.'<br /> <br /> That said, just because Mages think their views are superior does not mean that they are authoritarian in how they spread them. As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24689\" data-vbnamecard=\"24689\">Kakost</a> said, sharing views and educating people is a method many Mages pursue and both of them *can* be done honestly and openly. The temptation to spread an idea in a heavy handed, imperialistic, or violent way is a constant temptation to Mages, I'll freely admit, but many Mages are morally and paradigmatically opposed to that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to disagree here strongly. I believe that you speak of is an <i>aspirational</i> goal for Mages, but that practically all of them as presented when we meet them in the game, PC action nonwhitstanding, are unable of it. This is quite clearly presented in all the Tradition books and Craft books, with the history of Magick, being a history of war, conflict and misunderstanding. Again, I don't believe this is down to them being Mages, but down to them being humans.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-01T12:16:27-07:00","id":1488729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1487577-victorian-mage-if-no-society-of-ether-then-who?p=1488721#post1488721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have to disagree here strongly. I believe that you speak of is an <i>aspirational</i> goal for Mages, but that practically all of them as presented when we meet them in the game, PC action nonwhitstanding, are unable of it. This is quite clearly presented in all the Tradition books and Craft books, with the history of Magick, being a history of war, conflict and misunderstanding. Again, I don't believe this is down to them being Mages, but down to them being humans.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think we are probably talking past each other on this. Violence and coercion are often prominent where there is conflict between ideology, I don't agree that means that Mages (or people in general) are incapable of spreading, sharing, or evaluating ideology without it. Dialogue, evangelization, rhetoric, debate, and inspiration are all things that exist and have changed the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-01T13:59:00-07:00","id":1488732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1487577-victorian-mage-if-no-society-of-ether-then-who?p=1488729#post1488729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I think we are probably talking past each other on this. Violence and coercion are often prominent where there is conflict between ideology, I don't agree that means that Mages (or people in general) are incapable of spreading, sharing, or evaluating ideology without it. Dialogue, evangelization, rhetoric, debate, and inspiration are all things that exist and have changed the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>I absolutely believe they are capable of it and should strive for it. I also believe they are not likely to do it by default as it clashes with the kind of head you need to be a Mage.That's the key reason why I feel most of the Trads would engage in a forceful stance towards sleepers as well as any opponents they may have for resources or reality zones*. This leads back to my original statement, Mage is quite a bit about being a stubborn asshole forcing a change on the world, and the Etherites are not especially egregious offenders here considering the company they keep.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">* I'd count evangelization as force as well, and one could argue that any debate performed by people with magical powers to make you trust them is slightly suspicious</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T04:04:13-07:00","id":1488785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1487577-victorian-mage-if-no-society-of-ether-then-who?p=1488732#post1488732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This leads back to my original statement, Mage is quite a bit about being a stubborn asshole forcing a change on the world, and the Etherites are not especially egregious offenders here considering the company they keep.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they aren't, but they are comfortable with specific forms of forcing the world that other Mages aren't and vice versa, and one of the forms Etherites are historically (and inspirationally) comfortable with is totalitarianism. Several other Traditions and Crafts are no less willing to force ideas on the world, but tend to idealize other methods like rule by the enlightened (Noocracy) or cultural supremacy. Still others are willing to use violence to destabilize the wrong systems but not force to impose the right ones (often because coercion actively interferes with people using their paradigm).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1487577-victorian-mage-if-no-society-of-ether-then-who?p=1488732#post1488732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:8px\">* I'd count evangelization as force as well...</span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:8px\">I would not, though if you are assuming that mind control is involved I can see why you would. I meant evangelization merely as public proclaiming, verbally or by example.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T04:18:28-07:00","id":1488789,"title":"","content":"Hey, Evangelization is NOT force or coercion. The first christians evangelized the mighty Roman Empire while they were being fed to the lions; it's impossible to claim that this evangelization was done by the use of violence, the christians were a powerless persecuted minority, and it began as a religion of slaves. Evangelization is vastly different from cultural imposition - and the person who's saying this (me) is an atheist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}